      "statement": "On a topologically separated analytic space, ordinary CLD forms admit ordinary-open moment descriptions by analytic units and Euclidean smooth superforms; scalar smooth functions locally have the form φ(t_f1,…,t_fm). These forms form an ordinary sheaf, and moment pullback commutes with wedge products, J, d′, and d″. Moment nullity is determined by restriction to compact moment images, and numerical equality determines equality of scalar sections. On a good Hausdorff analytic space, every compact subset inside an ordinary open admits an ordinary smooth compact cutoff equal to one nearby. A CLD (p,q)-form has support disjoint from every closed analytic subset of dimension less than max(p,q). CLD §§3.3–3.4, 6.2, and 15.1–15.2.",
