      "statement": "A pure n-dimensional topologically separated analytic space has a canonical positive calibrated integration theory, compatible with analytic-domain restriction. Its top-cell calibrations use actual finite-flat fibre-algebra degrees, including nilpotent lengths. Smooth top forms define signed Radon measures finite on compact moment domains; lower-dimensional cells carry no top measure. Integration over a pure closed analytic subspace equals integration over its associated cycle with actual generic Artinian multiplicities. Generic multiplicities are constant under domain restriction; at corresponding generic points of scalar extension, the upstairs multiplicity equals the original multiplicity times the multiplicity of the base-changed reduction. CLD 13.2.6–8, §§14.3–14.5, Theorem 15.7.1, and Proposition 16.6.3.",
