      "statement": "Let X be an analytic space of level n and L/K a complete analytic extension. Canonical calibrations satisfy π_*μ_L=μ. For a locally integrable tropically Borel (n,n) G-form ω, π_*ω_L,Rad=ω_Rad, with no field-degree factor. If F/K is finite and an F-analytic level-n space is viewed on the same carrier as K-analytic, its calibration is multiplied by [F:K]. For a morphism between level-n spaces finite outside a closed analytic subset of dimension less than n, the pushforward of the measure of a locally integrable pulled-back (p,n)-form, p=n−1 or n, equals its downstairs measure multiplied by the calibrated degree. CLD 14.3.6, Remark 14.4.3, and Propositions 15.3.1 and 15.4.3.",
