      "statement": "On locally differentially separated calibrated tropical spaces, positive CLD currents have coefficient Radon measures and admit locally bounded Borel multiplication. Integration currents are positive, and wedging with a strongly positive smooth form preserves positivity. Differentiation is weakly continuous and satisfies the smooth Leibniz rule; ordinary-open restriction and compact direct image commute with differentiation. Canonical integration on a boundaryless pure analytic space is d′- and d″-closed. Green’s formula and finite-domain inclusion-exclusion hold on compact calibrated domains with their induced boundary calibrations. CLD §§5.9–5.11, 7.2–7.3, and 7.7.",
