      "id": "1084f837-a67a-4f2f-8fcb-b24dde4a0bd9/7",
      "statement": "A stalkwise regular analytic function on a pure r-dimensional analytic space defines a pure codimension-one zero space with its effective associated divisor cycle. Let M be a compact pure r-dimensional analytic space satisfying S1, let T be a regular pure one-dimensional analytic space, and let f:M→T be pure of relative dimension r−1. For a unit moment b and a rigid t∈T, the calibrated top-dimensional fibre moment polyhedron is locally constant near t. If T=A¹ and t=0, the calibrated top-dimensional image of (b,f), for sufficiently negative log|f|, is the product of the actual calibrated zero-fibre polyhedron with the negative interval carrying standard primitive calibration. Source boundary is permitted. CLD 13.7.1 and Theorem 14.7.2 with target dimension one.",
