      "statement": "Let K be complete and nontrivially valued, X any strict separated pure one-dimensional K-analytic curve, and h:X→R continuous. Then h is GR harmonic if and only if h is G-locally real PL and every residue class L_h(x)∈Pic(red(X,x))_R is numerically trivial. Reduction, singularities, and nonreduced structures are permitted. GR Proposition 3.15.",
