      "id": "1084f837-a67a-4f2f-8fcb-b24dde4a0bd9/13",
      "statement": "On a good strict analytic space over a nontrivially valued field, a Λ-PL germ, where Λ=Z or Λ is divisible, has a well-defined residue class in Pic(red(X,x))_Λ, functorial under analytic morphisms, reduction, and scalar extension. It is semipositive at x exactly when its residue is nef, equivalently when it locally comes from a nef formal model; it is harmonic at x exactly when the residue is numerically trivial. For an already Λ-PL function, semipositivity and harmonicity pull back under analytic maps and descend globally under proper surjective maps, are equivalent under every complete analytic scalar extension, and are equivalent under reduction. The pointwise scalar converse additionally requires equality of the stated residue-field transcendence degrees. For separated finite-type schemes, nefness and numerical triviality are equivalent under field extension and reduction and descend under proper surjective maps. GJR §§6–7, especially Propositions 7.1 and 7.6.",
