      "id": "1084f837-a67a-4f2f-8fcb-b24dde4a0bd9/14",
      "statement": "Locally, a finite flat surjective morphism of good strict analytic spaces over a complete nontrivially valued field can be extended to admissible formal models, simultaneously dominating finitely many specified line-bundle models, and after admissible formal blowups can be made finite and flat on those models. The resulting finite flat modules are locally of finite presentation and hence locally free. Formal models admit common dominating blowups, and compact strict analytic domains can be realized as generic fibres of formal open subsets after admissible blowup. The formal-model lifting and flattening results invoked in GJR Proposition 5.11 and GM Proposition 2.7.",
      "url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/2111.05741v3",
