      "id": "1084f837-a67a-4f2f-8fcb-b24dde4a0bd9/15",
      "statement": "Let K be complete and nontrivially valued and X a strict rig-smooth K-analytic curve. A function h:X→R is GJR harmonic if and only if it is harmonic in Thuillier’s sense, including the semistable weighted-graph description after finite Galois extension. At an interior semistable vertex, the weighted sum of outgoing slopes of an integral model function equals the degree of its residue line bundle on the corresponding proper residual component. Real harmonic functions satisfy the same criterion by real linear extension. GJR Proposition 15.7 and its supporting slope comparison.",
