      "id": "1084f837-a67a-4f2f-8fcb-b24dde4a0bd9/17",
      "statement": "Let K be a complete non-Archimedean field and Γ⊆R_{>0} a subgroup with Γ·|K×| nontrivial. If X is a compact Γ-strict K-analytic space of dimension d and f_1,…,f_m are analytic units, its norm moment image is a finite polytope with rational exponents and constants in the divisible hull of Γ·|K×|, of dimension at most d. Its boundary image is contained in such a polytope of dimension at most d−1. Ducros, Espaces de Berkovich, polytopes, squelettes et théorie des modèles, Theorem 3.2, with its erratum.",
