      "id": "1084f837-a67a-4f2f-8fcb-b24dde4a0bd9/20",
      "statement": "An analytic morphism is without relative boundary at a germ exactly when its induced morphism of germ reductions is proper. Scalar extension of germ reductions is described by the corrected graded extension functor E_ψ for the induced map of graded residue fields. Relative interiors compose with equality when the intervening target morphism is locally separated. For admissible formal schemes over K°, a formal morphism is proper, respectively locally proper, exactly when its generic-fibre analytic morphism is proper, respectively without boundary. Temkin, Local Properties I, Corollary 4.4, and Local Properties II, Theorem 5.2, Lemma 5.3, and Corollary 5.7.",
