scalar extension nor proves positive-current regularization.  It identifies
those operations as distinct proof obligations and shows that a negative
answer to P06.2 produces a zero-current function outside the CLD-psh
hierarchy at the ground field.  In the pure-dimensional scope this would
disprove the missing nonsmooth converse in
\Cref{prop:cld-psh-positive-current}.

The following dated verification history explains those positive cases.
