      "summary": "Reconstructed strict maximal-residue finiteness through Tate division and Noether normalization, repairing audit premise 7. This is a foundational repair, not P06.2 recognition.",
      "detailedSummary": "A direct argument proves that maximal residues of strict Tate quotients are finite over the complete ground field. It also proves that zero-dimensional strict affinoids are finite-dimensional Artinian algebras with finitely many rigid analytic points. The proof does not assume the strict Nullstellensatz or field perfectness. Analytic point finiteness uses explicitly stated standard spectral foundations.",
      "text": "Let K be complete and non-Archimedean and T_n=K⟨X_1,…,X_n⟩. Every maximal ideal of a quotient of T_n has residue field finite over K. Every zero-dimensional strict K-affinoid algebra is finite-dimensional over K and Artinian. Its analytic carrier consists of finitely many rigid points. The algebraic assertions also hold for trivially valued K; the recognition assignment uses nontrivially valued K.\n\nHere is the reconstruction. For R=T_{n−1}, division by a monic polynomial p∈R[Y] whose coefficients have norm at most one gives polynomial quotient and remainder operators of norm at most one. Polynomial density extends these operators to R⟨Y⟩. Their identities, including uniqueness, persist by continuity. If f=p+e with ||e||<1, solve q=Q_p(g)−Q_p(eq) by contraction and put r=R_p(g−eq). This gives unique division g=fq+r, deg_Y r<deg p, and makes R⟨Y⟩/(f) a finite free R-module.\n\nEvery nonzero Tate series can be put in this distinguished form. Scale by a coefficient attaining its Gauss norm. Its reduction is a nonzero finite polynomial. Choose M larger than all its exponents and substitute X_i↦X_i+X_n^{M^i}, i<n. This triangular substitution and its inverse are bounded and therefore isometric. Base-M weights distinguish the finitely many reduced monomials. The unique monomial of greatest weight gives the highest X_n coefficient, whose reduction is a nonzero constant; all higher coefficients have norm strictly below one. Their supremum is strictly below one because the coefficients tend to zero. The highest coefficient is invertible by a geometric series. Multiplying by its inverse gives precisely the division situation above.\n\nInduction gives an injected Tate algebra T_d→A for every nonzero quotient A=T_n/I, with A finite over T_d: if I≠0, use one distinguished f∈I, pass through the finite T_{n−1}-module T_n/(f), and normalize T_{n−1}/ker(T_{n−1}→A). The same induction proves noetherianity: I/(f) is a submodule of a finite module over the noetherian T_{n−1}, and lifts of its finite generators together with f generate I.\n\nApply normalization to the field E=T_n/m. Finiteness implies integrality by the determinant trick on module generators. If a field is integral over an injected domain R, then R is a field: a monic equation for r^{-1}, multiplied by r^{N−1}, expresses r^{-1} in R. T_d is not a field when d>0, since evaluation X_1=0 has a proper nonzero kernel. Thus d=0 and E is finite over K. Maximal ideals of a quotient lift to maximal ideals of T_n.\n\nFor a zero-dimensional affinoid A, noetherianity gives finitely many minimal primes, which here are all the maximal ideals. Its finitely generated nilradical N is nilpotent. Chinese remaindering makes A/N a finite product of the finite residue fields just proved. Each N^j/N^{j+1} is a finite A/N-module. The resulting finite filtration proves finite K-dimension and Artinianity.\n\nThe analytic assertion uses the exact standard foundations stated in CLD 11.1.1–2 and 11.4.4: analytic spectra contain points over maximal ideals, affinoid spectra surject onto prime spectra, and finite affinoid algebras have their finite-module Banach topology. Each finite residue field is complete. Two extending absolute values are equivalent finite-dimensional K-norms; applying their comparison inequalities to z^q and taking q-th roots proves equality. Thus each maximal ideal supplies exactly one analytic point, and its completed residue field is finite. There are no other prime kernels in dimension zero.\n\nThe full proof and primary foundation bodies are in P06.2-argument.md, section A and Appendix S, in /workspace/research/campaigns/round-17/P06.2-recognition-source-proof-repair/artifacts/codex-qg6o2s. Rebuild with python3 prepare.py. The corrected BGR locator is 6.1.2/3; no BGR statement or previous review is used as the proof. This repairs rigid exceptional-set finiteness but supplies no current ascent or harmonic recognition.",
