      "detailedSummary": "The repair assumes an already established annular collar and affine norm data there. A smooth maximum preserves Hessian positivity, agrees exactly with the original functions at one end and with a common affine function at the other. A Laurent-series argument extends affine Gauss norm identities to the whole annulus. Semistable chart construction and Wanner’s other model/comparison dependencies remain unproved here.",
      "text": "This is a local repair with explicit inputs. On an actual open annulus with logarithmic coordinate t∈(a,d), choose a<b<c<d. Suppose u_k^±=ℓ(t)+α_k^±, where ℓ is affine and 0≤α_k^-≤α_k^+≤δ_k→0. Here smooth psh means ordinary smooth with nonnegative ordinary CLD Hessian current. No nonsmooth regularization or classical curve-test recognition is asserted.\n\nFix ε>0 independently of δ_k, including when δ_k=0. Choose t_0∈(b,c) and M>0 with M(t_0−b)>3ε and M(c−t_0)>3ε. Put ψ=ℓ+M(t−t_0). For a nonnegative even smooth kernel supported in (−1,1), let θ_ε=|·|*ρ_ε and m_ε(A,B)=(A+B+θ_ε(A−B))/2. Convexity, Jensen’s inequality and the triangle inequality give |s|≤θ_ε(s)≤|s|+ε. The zero first moment makes θ_ε(s)=|s| when |s|≥ε. Its derivative lies in [−1,1], so m_ε is convex and nondecreasing in each argument, with each partial derivative at most one.\n\nSet w_k^±=m_ε(u_k^±,ψ). Both inputs are affine functions of the logarithm of an analytic unit. Their smoothed maximum has nonnegative second derivative in t, hence a positive smooth Hessian form. Boundaryless Stokes and the smooth current Leibniz rule identify its Hessian current with that form times canonical integration; the exact calculus statements and proofs are CLD 7.7.7–9, included in the appendix.\n\nFor δ_k<ε, on the left interval (a,b) the original input exceeds ψ by more than 3ε, so w_k^±=u_k^± exactly. On (c,d), ψ exceeds both original inputs by more than 2ε, so w_k^+=w_k^-=ψ exactly. These are identities on open end neighbourhoods: the differences glue to the original difference on the left and zero on the right without boundary derivative terms. Monotonicity makes the difference nonnegative. Also |m_ε(ℓ+α,ψ)−m_ε(ℓ,ψ)|≤|α|, so both functions converge uniformly to the same limit. If δ_k is zero, the same positive ε works and their difference is identically zero.\n\nThe skeletal-to-annular norm step must also be checked. Write an analytic annular function as a convergent Laurent series Σa_nT^n. If its finite Gauss logarithmic norm is affine throughout an open interval, any coefficient line touching that affine norm at an interior radius must have the same slope; otherwise it exceeds the norm on one side. The maximum is attained because coefficients decay on compact subannuli. Thus there is a unique maximizing exponent. At every analytic point of that radius the uniquely largest Laurent term cannot cancel. Consequently |f| equals its affine Gauss norm throughout the actual annulus, and f is a unit on compact subannuli.\n\nFor finitely many projective-coordinate ratios, choose a compact interval strictly inside an open edge on which all nonzero Gauss norms are affine and maximizing sets are constant. The Laurent argument gives the identities on the entire annulus. Nonmaximizing terms have a positive minimum gap there; Wanner’s deletion rule removes them for large k, leaving an affine function plus a constant in [0,1/k]. Adding 1/k to the positive approximant supplies the ordering above with δ_k≤2/k.\n\nThe erroneous source chart is τ^{-1}([y,x_e]) called a closed annulus although it can include a positive-genus skeletal vertex. Such a vertex cannot be an annular endpoint. The repair uses only a collar compactly inside the open edge, leaves the original functions near y, and trims the far side before another vertex. With finitely many disjoint collars, exact end identities permit common compact support and one threshold on k. The existence of those collars and affine data remains an input, not a constructed semistable model.\n\nThe complete local proof and Wanner’s relevant full proof bodies appear in section E and Appendix S of P06.2-argument.md. Run python3 prepare.py to rebuild. This does not establish Wanner’s full comparison chain, R0, two-sign ordinary psh regularization, or harmonic approximation.",
